? \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n It looks like these should be hitting their warehouses about now, and there’s an Amazon listing (with delivery a few weeks out), so I’ve been looking back at this.\n If you were to use a Sata+power extension cable, is there any reason this wouldn’t support a 3.5″ sata drive mounted externally? Would it be difficult to route the cable out of the front bays? \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n Opposite its cool, a nas that just does what we need, nas thing \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n Unfortunately I have been checking online for Australian compatible nas, the Synology 423+ is no longer available, only the 425 at $820 local currency. The ubiquity unas whilst is appealing is about $1200( 7 bays is rather overkill for my needs). Synology is favoured because I already use a Synology ds220j and the dsm software, but like many not to happy about the Lockout by Synology for non Synology branded , memory and hard drives and m.2 storage. \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n Based on your reviews of Ugreen NASs I recently bought a DXP 2800. I installed 2 x 6TB N300 Toshiba HDs and 2 x Samsung 256GB NVMes. I also upgraded the Ram to 16GB. I then ran into an issue that whenever I tied to do anything with the NAS it would shutdown with warnings about power interruptions. I did absolutely everything that I could think of to solve the problem and even resorted to buying a new PSU. I then decided to replace the 16GB of Crucial Ram that I’d installed with the 8GB of RAM that the NAS shipped with. So far that has completely solved the issues and the NAS is running normally. I’m quite happy with the performance of the 2800, especially with the N300s. Providing that the NAS proves reliable I’m really happy with it. \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n Am I the only one who gets 60+ Celsius on the CPU when idling on this thing? \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n Wonder what unifi are going to do as Time Machine is due to be deprecated soon? \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n data = dayerr \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n Thanks for the video. Can you create shareable links for NAS files in Explorer etc? Like with Dropbox, as a right click. What’s the Explorer integration if any? Cheers \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n I heard Ugreen’s hardware currently allows installing any 3rd party NAS OS of choice. Is there any signs that this capability might get blocked someday? \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n You do great videos for people like us who cannot afford the expensive tech items\n Nothing wrong with starting with any of these devices\n Maybe you should do a video on each off these items detailing what people could do with them. \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n This guy in every thumbnail: ???? \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n Bro, you can’t say the N word anymore. \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n I recently bought a Ugreen 4800 plus on prime day thinking of saving some bucks. However I made the mistake of not ordering HDDs and NVMEs. Now the prices on those are sky rocketed. So I am going to return the NAS unopened and wait for deal on HDDs to come by then purchasing the NAS in future. \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n what watch is that? the golden one is that extra solar panel? \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n I HAVE THE SAME WATCH! I love it. Its such a cool conversation piece. \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n Thanks for the video! Love the Street Fighter 2 thing there. Any video is just better with SF2 samples \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n I like to see shr features in this and 10 gbe r45 port. Its so close to totally replacing synology. For a 7 bay its half the price of synology nas \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n “This little MOFO”, oh my, I couldn’t stop laughing! Thanks, I needed that! \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n Can you mix disk sizes and brands in a logical volume?\n With Synology going proprietary disks I’m looking for someone who lets me mix and match as capacities increase, hopefully with 10 gb NICs built-in. \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n If you are consider beelink mini but want more powerful version, you can wait a bit, they already said they will bring a PRO or MAX version \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n Why are so few in a rack mount shape? \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n I decided to buy UGREEN NASync DXP4800 Plus. The first thing I tried was Coud Sync – doesn’t work at all. It doesn’t work with Google Drive, it doesn’t work with Microsoft OneDrive neither. I’m returning it. Ridiculous \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n Uh oh don’t let Synology see this otherwise they’ll make it so you can’t benchmark third party drives! Like how you can’t see detailed SMART info for third party drives ????\n I think Synology’s idea with the drive restrictions is so that they can better support problems since the drives run their own firmware and are supposedly better optimised to work with the enclosure/filesystem/SHR etc. Would be curious to know if that’s actually the case though. I did see someone on Reddit saying Synology drives throw fewer errors in their enterprise systems. \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n Went to uGreen. (I have been Syno user since 2013) RIP Syno. \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n Orico CF500 Pro (479) vs Ugreen DS4800Plug (512) which is a better buy?? \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n The G9 can run hot and susceptible to throttling, correct? Would be ideal otherwise. \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n Is it possible to replace the wifi card in the Beelink ME Mini for boot ssd? \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n Yes… sitting on decades of media… that’s DEFINITELY why I use Plex!…… \n REPLY ON YOUTUBE \n Loading... \n At one point during my Synology Vs Ugreen NAS decision process, I was strongly considering the DXP2800 to get my foot into the door of UGOS and Ugreen devices. However, I’ve seen on Readit some accounts of that model overheating